This repository is a derivative work. It extends the code released with:

  Fredin Haslum, J., Lardeau, C.-H., Karlsson, J., Turkki, R., Leuchowius, K.-J.,
  Smith, K. & Muellers, E.
  Cell Painting-based bioactivity prediction boosts high-throughput screening
  hit-rates and compound diversity.
  Nature Communications 15, 3470 (2024). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-47171-1

Original code: https://github.com/cfredinh/bioactive
Original license: Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE, unchanged).
All credit for the original data pipeline, assay setup, training code and the
published benchmark belongs to the original authors.

Changes and additions made in this repository:
  - Frozen foundation-model embeddings with trained heads (DINOv2, DINOv3,
    CLIP, BiomedCLIP, Cell-DINO) evaluated on the six Butina folds.
  - Statistical analysis of the cross-validation results (Friedman, Wilcoxon).
  - Brightfield-only and fluorescence adaptation experiments.
  - Explainability analysis: Grad-CAM, ViT-CX, occlusion, per-channel ablation,
    centre-box control and a foreground/background masking test.
  - Cluster job generators, verification script and result tables.
  - Reorganisation of the files into the folder layout described in README.md.
A file-by-file comparison with the original repository is in docs/UPSTREAM_COMPARISON.md.

Third-party data (JUMP-CP, ChEMBL) is subject to its own terms.
